cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research record, please cite it."
title: "Is there a genuine gap in CI/CD regression testing for quantum software? A primary-source-verified prior-art study"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Sadeqi"
    given-names: "Said Mohaddes"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sadeqisaidmohaddes-star/quantum-cicd-research"
url: "https://quantum.sadeqi.me/research"
abstract: >
  A prior-art investigation into whether an open-source, pytest-native, cross-SDK
  regression/equivalence-testing infrastructure for quantum software exists. Fourteen
  claims are checked against primary sources (official repositories, arXiv, DOI records),
  twenty-two prior-art systems are inspected, and the original hypothesis is narrowed:
  cross-version regression testing already exists (QUTest), pytest-native cross-SDK
  harnesses exist for benchmarking (Benchpress), and the surviving gap is pytest-native
  cross-SDK equivalence/regression detection — addressed by the companion tool pytest-qequiv.
keywords:
  - quantum software engineering
  - regression testing
  - continuous integration
  - equivalence checking
  - prior art
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-08-21
version: 1.0.0
